.SS " Iterator[str] packaging\&.tags\&.android_platforms (int | None  api_level = \fCNone\fP, str | None  abi = \fCNone\fP)"

.PP
.nf
Yields the :attr:`~Tag\&.platform` tags for Android\&. If this function is invoked on
non-Android platforms, the ``api_level`` and ``abi`` arguments are required\&.

:param int api_level: The maximum `API level
    <https://developer\&.android\&.com/tools/releases/platforms>`__ to return\&. Defaults
    to the current system's version, as returned by ``platform\&.android_ver``\&.
:param str abi: The `Android ABI <https://developer\&.android\&.com/ndk/guides/abis>`__,
    e\&.g\&. ``arm64_v8a``\&. Defaults to the current system's ABI , as returned by
    ``sysconfig\&.get_platform``\&. Hyphens and periods will be replaced with
    underscores\&.

.fi
.PP
 
.SS " Iterator[\fBTag\fP] packaging\&.tags\&.compatible_tags (\fBPythonVersion\fP | None  python_version = \fCNone\fP, str | None  interpreter = \fCNone\fP, Iterable[str] | None  platforms = \fCNone\fP)"

.PP
.nf
Yields the sequence of tags that are compatible with a specific version of Python\&.

The tags consist of:
- py*-none-<platform>
- <interpreter>-none-any  # \&.\&.\&. if `interpreter` is provided\&.
- py*-none-any

.fi
.PP
 
.SS " Iterator[\fBTag\fP] packaging\&.tags\&.cpython_tags (\fBPythonVersion\fP | None  python_version = \fCNone\fP, Iterable[str] | None  abis = \fCNone\fP, Iterable[str] | None  platforms = \fCNone\fP, *bool  warn = \fCFalse\fP)"

.PP
.nf
Yields the tags for a CPython interpreter\&.

The tags consist of:
- cp<python_version>-<abi>-<platform>
- cp<python_version>-abi3-<platform>
- cp<python_version>-none-<platform>
- cp<less than python_version>-abi3-<platform>  # Older Python versions down to 3\&.2\&.

If python_version only specifies a major version then user-provided ABIs and
the 'none' ABItag will be used\&.

If 'abi3' or 'none' are specified in 'abis' then they will be yielded at
their normal position and not at the beginning\&.

.fi
.PP
 
.SS " Iterator[\fBTag\fP] packaging\&.tags\&.generic_tags (str | None  interpreter = \fCNone\fP, Iterable[str] | None  abis = \fCNone\fP, Iterable[str] | None  platforms = \fCNone\fP, *bool  warn = \fCFalse\fP)"

.PP
.nf
Yields the tags for a generic interpreter\&.

The tags consist of:
- <interpreter>-<abi>-<platform>

The 'none' ABI will be added if it was not explicitly provided\&.

.fi
.PP
 
